+   -- System 573 (psx_patches/0026): the PSX controller state machine (joypad_pad,
+   -- the digital/analog/DualShock/GunCon/neGcon/mouse/Justifier SIO0 device, ~534 ALM)
+   -- is removed. The 573 is a JAMMA/JVS arcade board: it has NO PSX controller port,
+   -- and gameplay input arrives over the JAMMA register in s573_io.v (0x1f400008,
+   -- fed by emu.sv ~{joy}), entirely independent of this SIO0 pad path. The PS1
+   -- memory cards (joypad_mem below) are KEPT -- DDR/Dancing-Stage edit data saves to
+   -- the PS1 card. The pad's contributions to the shared SIO0 OR-bus are tied to
+   -- benign idle so the bus reads exactly as if no pad device is present:
+   --   receiveValidPad = 0 -> OR-bus receiveValid unaffected by the (absent) pad
+   --   receiveBufferPad = 0 -> OR into receiveBuffer is a no-op
+   --   ackPad           = 0 -> OR into ack is a no-op (no spurious SIO0 ack)
+   --   isActivePad      = 0 -> the memcard slotIdle (not isActivePad) stays asserted
+   -- The pad-only outputs (padMode, joypadN_rumble, JustifierIrqEnable) are tied to
+   -- their reset/idle constants. irqRequest (the JOY/SIO0 IRQ7 line) is unaffected:
+   -- it is driven by the process from JOY_CTRL(12)/waitAck, which only assert when a
+   -- device acks -- with no pad and no card transfer, it never fires.
+   isActivePad        <= '0';
+   receiveValidPad    <= '0';
+   receiveBufferPad   <= (others => '0');
+   ackPad             <= '0';
+   padMode            <= "00";
+   joypad1_rumble     <= (others => '0');
+   joypad2_rumble     <= (others => '0');
+   joypad3_rumble     <= (others => '0');
+   joypad4_rumble     <= (others => '0');
+   JustifierIrqEnable <= "00";
+   ss_out(7)          <= (others => '0');
+
